WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:16.139
Tommy Stubbins had big dreams.

2
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.903
He dreamt of one day visiting faraway lands and seeing the world.

3
00:00:20.904 --> 00:00:26.504
But for now, his life was in Puddleby, where nothing much exciting happened.

4
00:00:26.505 --> 00:00:28.701
"Tommy, take these to Colonel Bellowes.

5
00:00:28.702 --> 00:00:33.417
And be quick about it!" his father urged.

6
00:00:33.418 --> 00:00:36.307
Tommy's father was the shoemaker in Puddleby.

7
00:00:36.308 --> 00:00:39.660
He wanted Tommy to follow in his footsteps.

8
00:00:39.661 --> 00:00:44.892
But Tommy was not interested in fixing shoes.

9
00:00:44.893 --> 00:00:47.864
People like Colonel Bellowes upset him.

10
00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:51.174
"Your shoes, sir," Tommy said, smiling.

11
00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:54.137
The colonel rudely grabbed the shoes.

12
00:00:54.138 --> 00:00:57.375
Tommy wanted to kick the door.

13
00:00:57.376 --> 00:01:02.129
Fortunately, before Tommy could do that, a sound caught his attention.

14
00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.638
He found a wounded squirrel.

15
00:01:04.639 --> 00:01:10.186
Tommy was not fond of mean men like the Colonel, but he did love animals.

16
00:01:10.187 --> 00:01:13.264
"You poor thing," he said gently.

17
00:01:13.265 --> 00:01:18.092
He could not see what was causing the squirrel pain.

18
00:01:18.093 --> 00:01:20.938
Tommy decided to take the squirrel home.

19
00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:25.905
Along the way, he ran into Matthew, a friendly old man he knew.

20
00:01:25.906 --> 00:01:29.961
"What have you got there, Tommy?" Matthew pointed.

21
00:01:29.962 --> 00:01:35.383
"A squirrel, but I don't know what's wrong with it," he answered.

22
00:01:35.384 --> 00:01:39.676
"You need to see Dr. Dolittle," Matthew advised.

23
00:01:39.677 --> 00:01:42.964
"Who is he? Is he a vet?" asked Tommy.

24
00:01:42.965 --> 00:01:45.447
Matthew looked shocked.

25
00:01:45.448 --> 00:01:49.293
"He's better than a vet!" he exclaimed.

26
00:01:49.294 --> 00:01:55.241
"One time, my duck Lulu was sick, so I took her to see the doctor."

27
00:01:55.242 --> 00:01:58.200
"What was the matter with her?" Tommy asked.

28
00:01:58.201 --> 00:02:01.216
"Be patient. I'm getting to that part."

29
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:05.759
Matthew cleared his throat.

30
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:12.577
"John Dolittle used to be a human doctor, but he realized he wanted to help animals."

31
00:02:12.578 --> 00:02:16.530
"Like me! I like helping animals, too."

32
00:02:16.531 --> 00:02:21.686
"Do you want to hear this story or not?" Matthew sighed loudly.

33
00:02:21.687 --> 00:02:25.218
"Oops! Sorry," Tommy apologized.

34
00:02:25.219 --> 00:02:29.075
"Not only does Dr. Dolittle help animals,"

35
00:02:29.076 --> 00:02:32.838
Matthew said, then lowered his voice mysteriously,

36
00:02:32.839 --> 00:02:36.333
"but he can speak their language, too!"

37
00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:40.358
"What?!" Tommy shouted.

38
00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:43.354
Matthew told Tommy the whole story.

39
00:02:43.355 --> 00:02:46.587
Dr. Dolittle had examined Matthew's duck.

40
00:02:46.588 --> 00:02:51.033
"You have a very bad throat," the doctor had told Lulu.

41
00:02:51.034 --> 00:02:53.588
"You mustn't quack so loudly."

42
00:02:53.589 --> 00:02:55.239
"But I can't help it!

43
00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:00.873
Those cows keep coming to my pond!" quacked Lulu.

44
00:03:00.874 --> 00:03:03.944
"Dr. Dolittle and the duck talked to each other?"

45
00:03:03.945 --> 00:03:06.218
Tommy could not believe it.

46
00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:10.834
Matthew nodded. "They made strange clucking sounds."

47
00:03:10.835 --> 00:03:14.235
"Could you understand it?" asked Tommy.

48
00:03:14.236 --> 00:03:16.871
Matthew shook his head.

49
00:03:16.872 --> 00:03:19.485
"No, I don't have the gift.

50
00:03:19.486 --> 00:03:23.929
Dr. Dolittle had to explain to me what they talked about."

51
00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:28.749
Then, Matthew said, the doctor wrote something on a slip of paper.

52
00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:33.706
"Lulu, I'm going to give this to Matthew," the doctor said.

53
00:03:33.707 --> 00:03:36.411
"What is it?" quacked Lulu.

54
00:03:36.412 --> 00:03:44.517
"Every day you must drink juice made of barley, grass, onions, and carrots," Dr. Dolittle explained.

55
00:03:44.518 --> 00:03:49.163
"Yuck! Quack!" shrieked Lulu.

56
00:03:49.164 --> 00:03:53.073
"Lulu!" Dr. Dolittle said sternly.

57
00:03:53.074 --> 00:03:58.062
"Uh, doctor, is she all right?" Matthew was worried.

58
00:03:58.063 --> 00:04:04.793
"Yes, Matthew. Just make sure she drinks this juice every day," said the doctor.

59
00:04:04.794 --> 00:04:08.071
"Did the juice work?" Tommy wanted to know.

60
00:04:08.072 --> 00:04:12.728
"Lulu was back to normal in a few days," Matthew replied.

61
00:04:12.729 --> 00:04:15.067
Matthew began walking again.

62
00:04:15.068 --> 00:04:16.981
Tommy walked beside him.

63
00:04:16.982 --> 00:04:21.276
"I wonder if he can help this squirrel?" Tommy asked hopefully.

64
00:04:21.277 --> 00:04:24.647
"John Dolittle can do it," said Matthew.

65
00:04:24.648 --> 00:04:28.436
"But I'm afraid he's not here right now."

66
00:04:28.437 --> 00:04:30.608
"Where is he?" Tommy asked.

67
00:04:30.609 --> 00:04:33.333
"Well, he's on a voyage, of course.

68
00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:37.670
He loves to travel the world!" Matthew exclaimed.

69
00:04:37.671 --> 00:04:40.094
Tommy's eyes got bright.

70
00:04:40.095 --> 00:04:44.886
"I wonder if one day I can travel with him?" he said aloud.

71
00:04:44.887 --> 00:04:51.642
Unknown to Tommy, his wish would soon come true.
